And the lenses themselves become a library

PatternDex should maintain LensDex alongside PatternDex.

Not thousands of metaphors. A compact set of transformations with known affordances:

\begin{array}{c|c}
\text{Lens} & \text{Good at revealing}\\
\hline
Genome & generative specification\\
Development & timing/choreography\\
Evolution & selection/variation\\
Ecology & interaction/niches\\
Immune & anomaly/self distinction\\
Neural & distributed representation\\
Music & relational invariance/time\\
Dance & dynamic relational state\\
Map & purpose-relative compression\\
Chemistry & emergent composition\\
Architecture & structural constraint\\
Game & incentive/objective dynamics\\
Market & distributed valuation\\
Optics & observer/filter effects\\
Mycelium & unguided local exploration\\
Language & compositional transmission\\
Code & explicit execution\\
Math & relational manipulation
\end{array}

Then when I’m stuck:

\texttt{PARALLAX}(problem,
[\text{genome,music,map,game}])

Compare.

Harvest only deltas.

And PatternDex learns which lenses reveal useful structure for which problem classes.

Eventually:

(\text{problem signature})
\rightarrow
\text{Metamap}
\rightarrow
\text{best lens ensemble}

So we aren’t merely accumulating analogies.

We’re building a multi-instrument scientific apparatus for meaning.

And the highest-leverage deltas from this first run are, to me:

Environmental Subtraction — don’t encode what the receiver/environment reliably supplies.

Operator Choreography — sequence/timing is itself part of the program.

Semantic Constellations — important mechanisms should have multiple reconstructive addresses.

Semantic Transposition — change every surface element while preserving relational intervals to test a Seal.

Relational State — some information exists between entities over time, not inside either.

Goal-Relative Compression — there is no minimum representation independent of intended use.

Neutral Variation — exploration must sometimes occur before a fitness direction is chosen.

Architectural Instruction — make environment/topology perform instruction so tokens don’t have to.

And PARALLAX ties the whole operation together:

Don’t merely change your answer. Change the medium that is allowed to answer—and study the disagreement.

That’s a serious addition to the PatternDex.